<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>Campus Cafe - College Name</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f7f7f7;
            margin: 30px;
        }
        .section {
            padding: 15px;
            background-color: #ffffff;
            border: 1px solid #ddd;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }
        h1, h2 {
            color: #2c3e50;
        }
        hr {
            border: 1px solid #ccc;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <div class="section">
        <h1>🍵 Campus Cafe</h1>
        <p>Welcome to the Campus Cafe at <strong>XYZ College</strong>. We serve fresh coffee, snacks, and meals every day for students and staff.</p>
    </div>

    <hr>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>📅 Opening Hours</h2>
        <p>Monday to Friday:<br> 7:00 AM – 8:00 PM</p>
        <p>Saturday:<br> 8:00 AM – 3:00 PM</p>
        <p>Sunday: Closed</p>
    </div>

    <hr>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>🍽️ Menu Highlights</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Espresso & Cappuccino</li>
            <li>Veg Sandwich & Chicken Wrap</li>
            <li>Fruit Bowl & Yogurt</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <hr>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>📍 Location</h2>
        <p>The cafe is located beside the college library building.<br>Address: Block C, XYZ College, Kathmandu</p>
    </div>

    <hr>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>🖥️ Static vs. Dynamic Page Use</h2>
        <p>
            <strong>This page is static</strong> — it shows the same cafe information to every visitor.<br>
            <br>
            If we wanted to show today's special menu based on a database, or allow students to place orders online,
            we’d use a <strong>dynamic web page</strong>.
        </p>
    </div>

</body>
</html>
